Z||000000||rodmcneill||03-12-2001||02:16 AM||||I just noticed something for the first time tonight while checking out Ebay. There are a couple of guys selling the 88 Fiero GT poster, the one with the red GT in it. The car in the poster has either had the front suspension lowered or the photo has been "doctored". I have a 88 GT myself and one thing I don't like about the 88's is that the front end was jacked up by at least 1" over previous models. This as well as other mods. gives more wheel travel to the 88's. It just bugs me that GM realised that the vehicle looked better with the front end lowered and did this for their advertising. Has anyone else ever noticed this, or is this a little trickery being discovered 13 years later?||||reg||5
